  "articleBody": "Planning your tiny home project can be exciting, but some common slip-ups can turn that excitement into frustration. Here are a few mistakes to sidestep:\n\n*   **Mistake 1: Not clarifying your lifestyle needs first.** \n    *   *How to avoid it:* Before looking at floor plans, think deeply about how you use space daily. Do you work from home? Love to cook? Need a lot of storage? Zen Tiny Homes focuses on this from day one to create a truly custom fit.\n*   **Mistake 2: Only focusing on square footage, not livability.** \n    *   *How to avoid it:* A smaller home doesn't mean less livable. Prioritize smart layouts and multi-functional areas. We excel at making compact footprints feel open and personal.\n*   **Mistake 3: Overlooking storage solutions.** \n    *   *How to avoid it:* Tiny homes need smart storage. Don't forget built-ins, vertical space, and clever nooks. Our designs integrate meaningful storage seamlessly.\n*   **Mistake 4: Not considering the end-to-end process.** \n    *   *How to avoid it:* From initial concept to move-in, understand all the phases. Our simplified process covers property assessment, design, and construction, so you're never in the dark.\n*   **Mistake 5: Treating it like a regular home build.** \n    *   *How to avoid it:* Tiny homes have unique design and construction needs. Work with specialists who understand compact living. That's our specialty at Zen Tiny Homes, with over a decade of experience.",
  "datePublished": "2026-09-02"
